{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{x^2+6x}{10-x^2}$ is a rational expression.\n\nTo find the derivative of rational expressions, we use **the quotient rule**:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac{u(x)}{v(x)}\\right]\u0026=\\dfrac{\\dfrac{d}{dx}[u(x)]v(x)-u(x)\\dfrac{d}{dx}[v(x)]}{[v(x)]^2}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{u'(x)v(x)-u(x)v'(x)}{[v(x)]^2}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's differentiate!\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{dy}{dx}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(\\dfrac{x^2+6x}{10-x^2}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{(10-x^2)\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^2+6x)-(x^2+6x)\\dfrac{d}{dx}(10-x^2)}{(10-x^2)^2}\\qquad\\gray{\\text{The quotient rule}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{(10-x^2)(2x+6)-(x^2+6x)(-2x)}{(10-x^2)^2}\\qquad\\gray{\\text{Differentiate }(x^2+6x)\\text{ \u0026 }(10-x^2)}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{20x+60-2x^3-6x^2+2x^3+12x^2}{(10-x^2)^2}\\qquad\\gray{\\text{Expand}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{6x^2+20x+60}{(10-x^2)^2}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{6x^2+20x+60}{(10-x^2)^2}$, or any other equivalent form.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $y=\\dfrac{x^2+6x}{10-x^2}$.\n\n$\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":"0","simplify":false,"value":"\\frac{6x^{2}+20x+60}{\\left(10-x^{2}\\right)^{2}}"}],"buttonSets":["basic","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"static":false,"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
